summary.value:
The paper focuses on the issues of limited data for a fine-grained downstream task and limited inference budget, and introduces a method called (Synthesize-Initialize-Distill CLIP) (SIDCLIP), involving three components: 
- Synthesize (S): a novel approach to generate synthetic data by leveraging CLIP;
- Initialize (I): model initialization of a smaller CLIP model pretrained on the target architecture; 
- Distill (D): knowledge distillation to a larger model. 
Experimental results are reported on three task-specific image classification datasets: StanfordCars, OxfordFlowers, and Food101.

